card.statement:
Let $\mathcal C=(\mathcal{C}_1,\mathcal{C}_2)$ be admissible.

- [(i)] We will say that a tableau $[l]$ of $\gl(m|n)$ satisfies $\mathcal{C}_1$ if:

- [$\bullet$] $l_{ij}-l_{rs}\in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$ for any $((i,j); (r,s))\in \mathcal{C}_1^+$;

- [$\bullet$] $l_{ij}-l_{rs}\in \mathbb{Z}_{> 0}$ for any $((i,j); (r,s))\in \mathcal{C}_1^-\cup\mathcal{C}_1^0$;

- [$\bullet$] For any $1\leq k\leq n$ we have, $l_{ki}-l_{kj}\in \mathbb{Z} $ if and only if $(k,i)$ and $(k,j)$ are in the same connected component of $G(\mathcal{C}_1)$.

- [(ii)] We will say that $[l]$ of $\gl(m|n)$ satisfies $\mathcal{C}_2$ if:

- [$\bullet$] $l_{ij}-l_{rs}\in \mathbb{Z}_{\leq 0}$ for any $((i,j); (r,s))\in \mathcal{C}_2^+\cup\mathcal{C}_2^0$;

- [$\bullet$] $l_{ij}-l_{rs}\in \mathbb{Z}_{< 0}$ for any $((i,j); (r,s))\in \mathcal{C}_2^-$;

- [$\bullet$] For any $m+1\leq k\leq m+n$ we have, $l_{ki}-l_{kj}\in \mathbb{Z} $ if and only if $(k,i)$ and $(k,j)$ are in the same connected component of $G(\mathcal{C}_2)$.

- [(iii)] We say that a tableau $[l]$ of $\gl(m|n)$ satisfies $\mathcal{C}$ if:

- $[l]$ satisfies $\mathcal C_1$ and $\mathcal C_2$;

- $\l_{ki}-\l_{k-1,i}\equiv\theta_{k-1,i}(l)\in\{0,1\}, 1\leq i\leq m, m+1\leq k\leq m+n$;

- $\l_{ki}- \l_{kj}\neq 0$ for $m+1\leq k\leq m+n-1$, $1\leq i\leq m<j \leq k$;

- If $[l']$ satisfies conditions (1)-(2) and ${l'}_{ki}={l}_{ki}+z_{ki}$, where $z_{ki}\in \mathbb Z$, $z_{m+n,i}=0$ for all $i$, then $[l']$ satisfies condition (3).
